# Browser support target. WITHOUT this file Angular falls back to its default
# ("last 2 versions" etc.), which resolved to iOS Safari 18.5+ ONLY — so the
# build emitted syntax and APIs that older iPhones cannot run.
#
# The symptom was not a visible error: the page rendered, but bootstrap threw
# and every button went dead. Navigation, dropdowns and links all silently did
# nothing on iPhone 6 and 7, while iPhone 11/13 were fine.
#
# Two concrete breakages that were shipping:
#   - `??=` / `||=` (logical assignment) — needs iOS 14+. A PARSE error on
#     iOS 12, so the whole file fails to load and no JS runs at all.
#   - `Object.hasOwn` — needs iOS 15.4+. A runtime throw during bootstrap.
#
# FLOOR IS iOS 15, NOT LOWER, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
# iOS 15 is the iPhone 7's last supported version, so the 7 is covered. The
# iPhone 6 (iOS 12) is NOT: esbuild refuses to build for it —
# "Transforming destructuring to the configured target environment (ios12.0)
# is not supported yet". Reaching iOS 12 would mean adding a Babel pass over
# the whole bundle, which is a real cost for a phone discontinued in 2016.
# Revisit only if iPhone 6 traffic proves material.
#
# Customers queueing at a salon skew toward older handsets, so this floor is
# worth keeping low — do not let it drift back up to "last 2 versions".
last 2 versions
> 0.5%
